## Original Content
Arabica coffee prices hit a record level, as traders digested the withdrawal of President Trump’s threats to impose tariffs and economic sanctions on Colombia.

## Summary
Arabica coffee prices have reached a record level following the withdrawal of President Trump's threats to impose tariffs and economic sanctions on Colombia. This development has prompted traders to adjust their positions in response to reduced trade tensions.

## Key Points
- Arabica coffee prices hit a record high.
- The surge is linked to the removal of U.S. tariff threats on Colombia.
- Traders are digesting the implications of reduced trade conflict.


